                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5379527c-930b-4551-a553-c2a3256bc8a3",
                                "sense_id": "8a71bc67-5640-315c-b032-5c168d8ee106",
                                "text": "when great Aunt Ryder was exhausted with carrying her little nephews pick-a-back, Aunt Ellen was always willing to become a 'gee-gee' or riding-horse in her place, although certainly one of no very prancing and fiery temperament."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "42594705-f178-4927-9d83-3ee3b0307499",
                                "sense_id": "8a71bc67-5640-315c-b032-5c168d8ee106",
                                "text": "But what was the good of saying that to him when he was on his high horse — a very prancing steed?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a9853e8-63fd-4a97-9d9e-50fa0f3c0428",
                                "sense_id": "8a71bc67-5640-315c-b032-5c168d8ee106",
                                "text": "he jammed his second-best sword into the empty scabbard; he ordered out his wildest, tallest, most prancing and dancing parade horse"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
